  "historical_output_text": " How to Start Seeds Indoors\n\n**How to Start Seeds Indoors**\n\nStarting seeds indoors is a great way to get a head start on your gardening season, especially if you live in a cooler climate or have a short growing season. Here’s a step-by-step guide to help you successfully start your seeds indoors.\n\n1. **Choose the Right Containers:**\n   Start by selecting the appropriate containers. You can use small plastic pots, peat pots, or even egg cartons. The goal is to provide a stable and sterile environment for your seeds to grow. Use containers that have drainage holes to prevent waterlogging, which can lead to seed rot.\n\n2. **Prepare the Growing Medium:**\n   Use a high-quality seed starting mix. This is different from regular potting soil because it’s lighter and free of pathogens that can harm young seedlings. Fill your containers with the seed starting mix, leaving about 1/4 inch of space at the top. Lightly press down the mix to ensure good contact with the seeds.\n\n3. **Plant the Seeds:**\n   Follow the specific planting depth and spacing instructions on the seed packet. Generally, seeds should be",
